## Corrected Traffic Flows

### 1. EC2 (Private) to RDS (Private) — Same VPC
\\\
EC2 to Private Subnet Route Table to Local Route (10.0.0.0/16) to RDS
\\\
- **No NAT Gateway**, **No Internet Gateway**
- Traffic stays entirely inside the VPC via the implicit local route

### 2. EC2 (Private) to Internet
\\\
EC2 to Private Route Table (0.0.0.0/0) to NAT Gateway (in Public Subnet)
    to Public Route Table (0.0.0.0/0) to Internet Gateway to Internet
\\\
- NAT Gateway **lives in the public subnet** but is **used by private subnets**
- Return traffic follows the same path in reverse (stateful)

