## Public vs Private Route Tables

| Route Table | Associated Subnets | Default Route (0.0.0.0/0) Target |
|-------------|-------------------|----------------------------------|
| **Public** | Public subnets | Internet Gateway |
| **Private** | Private subnets | NAT Gateway (in public subnet) |

> **Key distinction:** The NAT Gateway *resides* in a public subnet but *serves* private subnets. It uses the IGW to reach the internet.

